WHY THIS COPY EXISTS
--------------------
dsh-manager must be a self-contained plugin: it may not require the
@michengai/dsh-skills-manager plugin to be installed, and it may not load that
plugin at runtime. Its skill-management capabilities are therefore vendored
here as ordinary source files of this project.

WHAT WAS CHANGED
----------------
The vendored files are no longer byte-identical to upstream. The following
edits rebrand the code for this plugin. Each edit is a plain string or path
change; no algorithm, validation rule, or safety check was altered.

  1. identity      `name`'s value ("skills-manager") -> "dsh-manager"
  2. api prefix    API_PREFIX ("/api/michengai/dsh-skills-manager") -> "/api/manager"
  3. client header CLIENT_MARKER_HEADER ("x-dsh-skills-manager") -> "x-dsh-manager-client"
  4. state dir     managerHomePath() <DSH_HOME>/skills-manager -> <DSH_HOME>/manager
  5. log file      logPath() <DSH_HOME>/dsh-skills-manager.log -> <DSH_HOME>/manager/skills.log
  6. provider name "dsh-skills-manager-external" -> "manager-external"

Files removed from the vendored set: upstream `client.js` (its browser half is
replaced by this project's own UI) and upstream `client`-only locale JSON.

Per Apache-2.0 section 4(b), these modified files are marked as changed above.
Upstream's own copyright and license notices are retained in ./LICENSE and in
each file's original header comments.

UPGRADING
---------
`node scripts/check-vendored.mjs` records and verifies the SHA-256 of every
vendored file, so a future upstream bump can be diffed against exactly what is
in the tree today. See that script before replacing any file here.
